# Reboot without the firmware: load the next kernel from the running one.
#
# kexec-tools is one static-ish package with no daemon, no unit and no
# listening socket. It exists so `omarchy-server-update --kexec` can turn a
# required reboot into a jump straight into the signed UKI, skipping POST,
# device init, option ROMs and the bootloader menu -- on a virtual machine that
# is most of the reboot, and on real server hardware with a slow BMC it is
# nearly all of it.
#
# Not in the core, on the owner's premise that a package the machine does not
# need is a package it does not carry. A machine that reboots twice a year
# gains nothing from it; a fleet that updates nightly gains the difference
# between a five second gap and a ninety second one.
#
# omarchy-server-update-restart uses it only when it is present: with the addon
# absent, a required reboot is left as the upstream reboot-required marker and
# the operator's next window, exactly as before.
kexec-tools
